	(text "PWR_FLAG: supply enters through EP_FPC2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 150.495 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a1fc9504-07a7-5b81-85fd-b2ff4db40127")
	)
	(text "NOTES\n1. GDEY0213B74: SSD1680, 250x122, VCI 2.2-3.7V (3.3V here).\n   BS1 = GND -> 4-wire SPI, so EP_DC is required.\n2. Boost/charge pump = Good Display reference circuit:\n   L1 47uH (Isat >= 0.4A), Q1 Si1308EDL (alt. AO3400A, SOT-23),\n   D1-D3 MBR0530, R1 1M gate pull-down, R2 2.2 ohm RESE sense.\n   (2.2 ohm + 47uH suit SSD ICs; UC ICs use 0.47 ohm + 10uH.)\n3. Caps on PREVGH/PREVGL/VSH/VSL/VCOM must be rated >= 25V\n   (1uF/50V X5R; C8/C9 4.7uF/25V X5R).\n4. Pins 1/4 (NC), 6/7 (TSCL/TSDA), 19 (VPP) are left open.\n5. Stack-up: panel taped to the FRONT, every part on the BACK.\n   The panel FPC wraps 180 deg around the board edge into\n   EP_FPC1, so its gold fingers face AWAY from the PCB:\n   EP_FPC1 must be top- or dual-contact. AFC24-S24FIA-00 is\n   dual-contact, front-insert / rear-flip: the FPC enters on\n   the side opposite the pads, so face that side to the edge.\n   The bottom-contact AFC01 of the 1.02inch board won't mate.\n   Because of the fold, connector pad k = panel pin 25-k.\n6. EP_FPC2/EP_FPC3 pinout = 1.02inch-right EP_FPC2. They sit at\n   mirrored positions (x = +/-6 mm), same orientation, so one board\n   fits a left and a right half; the keyboard socket is mirrored.\n7. Keep the L1/Q1/R2/C8 loop tight; route PREVGH/PREVGL/VCOM\n   short and away from EP_CLK/EP_DIN; solid GND on the back.\n8. R3 (WS2812 data series R) may be 0R; EP_RGB1 is optional."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 116.84 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.2 1.2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "562d56ad-3251-5485-b62f-d73ad3114c0b")
	)
